                        "review": "Purchased this game around a decade ago and I finally got around to beating it today.\nIt might just be the way my mind works (poorly), but I found this game to be a bit more challenging than appearances would suggest. The encounter-by-encounter challenge isn't really all that to talk about, but it's more of the accumulative nature of fighting monsters, avoiding traps, and taking fall damage from not being careful enough. Add the fact that you begin with very little health, get (virtually no) assistance between attempts, and you lose all progress when you die, Eldritch ended up being a little grating at times. I don't mind a challenging game, and I think this one in particular sort of scratched the itch for \"try, try again\" gameplay in a way that worked for me. \nBeyond gameplay the sound design is decent, the environments are maybe no breathtaking but good, and the story doesn't really matter and isn't intrusive. \nAnyway, if \"HP Minecraft\" does something to tickle your brain, I'd recommend checking this one out. Maybe on a sale?",
